## Why This Is Asked
Assesses how a candidate combines deployment strategies, DR planning, and enforcement of security/compliance in a real GCP setup.

## Key Concepts
- Blue/Green and canary deployments with automatic rollback gates
- Cross-region DR for compute and database
- CMEK encryption for storage and Cloud SQL
- Policy-as-code and drift detection (Config Connector, OPA)
- Observability, outage handling, and compliance

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code for SLO gate
async function canaryGate(metrics) {
  const latencyOk = metrics.p95 < 200;
  const errorOk = metrics.errorRate < 0.01;
  return latencyOk && errorOk;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate drift detection in CI/CD and ensure fast remediations?
- What tests would you run to validate cross-region failover without customer-visible downtime?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design production-grade canaries with data-plane shadowing and multi-service integrations using Google-native tooling.

## Key Concepts
- Canary deployments with per-revision traffic
- Shadow traffic for data validation
- Pub/Sub driven sinks to BigQuery
- Cloud Monitoring alert policies and auto rollback
- Least-privilege IAM

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: emit prod request and publish shadow copy
async function handle(req){
  const prodResp = await prodEndpoint(req);
  await publishShadow(copyRequest(req));
  return prodResp;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you ensure idempotency and avoid double writes if shadow sink duplicates fail?
- How to test rollback safety and prevent drift between prod and shadow data?
